-- title:
--   Lemma 11 — Virtual-chain empty-set bound
-- statement:
--   For any QB-feasible flow and any subset I of active labels, the probability that all virtual coordinates in I are empty has a limit as time tends to infinity. This limit is bounded by the product of exp(−hatλ/(μ+sum passive rates)) over I. The virtual process is the empty-start process generated by (30)–(33), not a supplied family of random variables with an assumed bound.
--
--   Source statement:
--
--   For every $\mathcal I\subseteq\mathcal L^{>0}$, we have:
--   $$\lim_{t\to+\infty}\Pr\left[\sum_{(i,\ell)\in\mathcal I}\tilde X_t^{i,\ell}=0\right]\le\prod_{(i,\ell)\in\mathcal I}e^{-\frac{\hat\lambda_{i,\ell}}{\mu_i+\sum_{j\in S_i^\ell}\lambda^p_j}}.$$
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: a finite collection of arriving types → Fin n also permits the empty type graph; reason: the empty instance has zero rewards, flows and costs; restricting to nonempty graphs recovers every source instance
--   - encoding: compatibility indices 1 through the support size → zero-based indices with prefix length l+1; reason: the endpoints and all terms of every source sum are preserved
--   - generalization: a source-regime feasible flow satisfying the B.3 performance guarantee → any QB-feasible flow, also allowing mixed finite and immediate lifetime types; reason: these population comparisons do not need a reward guarantee; every source flow remains included
--   - reading: the virtual diagonal on PDF 48 is written as minus the sum over all states, including itself → the diagonal is minus the off-diagonal sum; reason: the ordinary generator and the coordinate generator on the same pages exclude the diagonal; conservativity fixes this evident index omission (I4)
-- source:
--   Aouad and Sarıtaç (2022), Dynamic Stochastic Matching Under Limited Time, https://doi.org/10.1287/opre.2022.2293, held published-basis manuscript, Lemma 11, printed p. 47 / PDF p. 48

import Definitions.Def_DynStochMatching_Reward_CountChains

open MeasureTheory Filter
open scoped ENNReal Classical

namespace DynStochMatching.Reward

theorem lemma_11 {n : ℕ} (D : Instance n) (x : Flow n)
    (hfeasible : qbFeasible D x) (I : Finset (LabelIndex n)) (hI : I ⊆ liveLabels x) :
    ∃ p : ℝ, Tendsto (emptyProbability D x I) atTop (nhds p) ∧
      p ≤ ∏ a ∈ I, Real.exp (-decomposition D x a.1 a.2.val /
        decompositionDenominator D x a.1 a.2.val) := by sorry

end DynStochMatching.Reward
